        "story_heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Every natural one let us down.&nbsp;",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "story_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>It began in a bathroom, with a drawer full of half-used tubes. Every natural deodorant either quit by lunchtime or left skin red and irritated — usually thanks to bicarb. Every one that actually worked was full of aluminium and things we couldn't pronounce.</p><p>\"Gentle <em>and</em> effective\" wasn't a product we could buy. So we spent two years making it — swapping bicarb for magnesium and testing balm after balm until it was kind to sensitive skin, smelled great, and lasted the whole day.</p>",
            "text_style": "subtitle"
          }
        }
      },
